# core/data/talk/grammar/en/grief_kids.tlk - T5b package T5B-GRIEF: grief and loss for and from children
# (owner: TK; K-10, SCRIPT_STYLE R6 and the cute filter, design 7.1 K-2). Two families of grief.* rules:
#   * a child speaks (guard kid_speaker, tags: nojoke,kid): short, simple, honest words a child would use;
#     no big idea about death, never graphic, never a joke, never a lesson. A child may be sad out loud
#     and may say no to a hug.
#   * an adult speaks with a child in the room (guard !kid_speaker&kid_present, tags: nojoke): warm,
#     simple, age-appropriate. The grown-up stays close, says the feeling is allowed, offers (never
#     presses) a hug, and says a grown-up will help. Nothing frightening, no detail, no joke.
# Same safety as grief.tlk: no register word, no catchphrase, no LOVE face, no [JMAT], no sub-rule,
# {lost} only where the rule can say it. Kids' banks: no cast name or voice (those are in grief_voices).

# ---- a child speaks -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.kid.answer act: answer guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "I'm sad. It's okay to be sad, right?"
  "It's a big feeling. It's too big for me sometimes."
  "I don't know what to say. I'm just sad."
  "My tummy feels funny when I think about it."
  "Sometimes I cry. Then I feel a bit better."
  "It's really hard. But I'm not alone. That helps."
@rule grief.kid.answer_lost act: answer guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "I miss {lost}. I miss {lost} lots."
  "[SAD]I look for {lost}. Then I remember."
@rule grief.kid.tell act: tell guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "I draw pictures when I'm sad. It helps."
  "I hug my pillow a lot. It's soft."
  "I'm trying to be brave. It's hard. I'm doing my best."
  "When it gets big, I count to ten. Sometimes twenty."
@rule grief.kid.tell_lost act: tell guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "I told {lost} goodnight. I know they can't hear. But I did."
@rule grief.kid.sympathize act: sympathize guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "I'm sorry. I'm really, really sorry."
  "That's so sad. I'm sad with you."
  "Oh no. I'm here. I'll stay."
  "I'm sorry. Do you want to sit with me?"
@rule grief.kid.comfort act: comfort guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "It's okay to cry. I cry too."
  "I'll sit with you. We don't have to talk."
  "You're not alone. I'm right here."
  "Want to hold my hand? You don't have to."
@rule grief.kid.backchannel act: backchannel guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "Mm. Okay. I'm here."
  "Yeah. I know."
  "I'm listening. Take your time."
@rule grief.kid.agree act: agree guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "Yeah. It's really sad."
  "I think so too."
@rule grief.kid.thank act: thank guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "Thank you. That was nice."
  "Thanks. I feel a little better."
  "Thank you for being nice to me."
@rule grief.kid.yes act: yes guard: kid_speaker&!act=ask_fact tags: nojoke,kid
  "Yes, please."
  "Yes. I'd like that."
@rule grief.kid.no act: no guard: kid_speaker&act=hug tags: nojoke,kid
  "No, thank you. Not right now. Maybe later?"
  "I don't want a hug now. I'm okay. Thank you."
@rule grief.kid.greet act: greet guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "Hi. I'm a bit sad today. It's okay."
@rule grief.kid.farewell act: farewell guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "Bye. Come back soon, okay?"
  "Bye. Thank you for talking to me."
@rule grief.kid.continue act: continue guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "You can tell me more. I'll listen."
@rule grief.kid.encourage act: encourage guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "Tell a grown-up you trust. They help."
  "Drink some water. It helps me."
@rule grief.kid.offer act: offer guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
  "You can sit with me. I'll share my blanket."
  "I could draw you a picture. Want one?"

# ---- a grown-up speaks, a child is in the room ------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.close.answer act: answer guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "It's okay to feel sad. It's okay to ask me anything."
  "It's sad. We'll go slowly. I'm right here."
  "You didn't do anything wrong. Nobody did. Remember that."
  "Big feelings come and go. We'll sit with them together."
  "I'm sad too. We can be sad together."
  "Thank you for asking. You can always ask me."
@rule grief.close.answer_lost act: answer guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "I miss {lost}. It's okay to miss people. It's a kind of love."
@rule grief.close.tell act: tell guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "When I'm sad, I go for a little walk. And I tell someone."
  "I look at a picture and I smile a little. Then I cry a little."
  "I drink some tea and I rest. Rest helps."
@rule grief.close.sympathize act: sympathize guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "I'm so sorry, sweetheart. I'm right here with you."
  "Oh, little one. I'm sorry. You're safe with me."
  "That's a very sad thing. It's okay to feel sad."
@rule grief.close.comfort act: comfort guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "You're safe. I'm here. We'll find a grown-up to help, too."
  "A hug is here if you want one. And if you don't, that's okay."
  "Cry as much as you like. Nobody will mind."
  "None of this is your fault. Not even a little bit."
@rule grief.close.encourage act: encourage guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "Draw a picture, or tell a story about them. It helps."
  "Talk to a grown-up you trust. Tell them how you feel."
  "Be kind to yourself. You're doing a good job."
@rule grief.close.offer act: offer guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "I'll sit with you. We can be quiet or we can talk."
  "I'll fetch you some water and a blanket. Is that okay?"
@rule grief.close.backchannel act: backchannel guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "I hear you. Take your time."
  "Yes. I understand. I'm listening."
@rule grief.close.thank act: thank guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "Thank you. That was very kind of you."
  "Thank you for being so caring."
@rule grief.close.farewell act: farewell guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present tags: nojoke
  "Goodbye for now. Come to me any time. I mean that."
@rule grief.close.no act: no guard: !kid_speaker&kid_present&act=hug tags: nojoke
  "Not right now, little one. Thank you. I'll take one later."
